        "date": "2026-11-24T04:54:40Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(motion): ring links only for ring sets, lift to the user's pass plane\n\nThe ring law of #3747 linked every area round a part with a chosen pass\nstart. It now links only the passes of a ring set (Waterline, Offset\nrings; `ring_links::rings`), so Zigzag rows keep their links of before\n#3818. The 2D Pocket with Outside containment keeps the ring law, with\npins: no overcut, no crossing feeds, each lift named, no lift round a\ndisc. The Adaptive fallback to Offset rings is pinned the same way.\n\nA failed ring link lifts to the clearance height when the user chose\nLink::Clearance for the pass link, and the link note names that plane.\nRetract, KeepDown and the default still lift to the retract plane.\n\nDecision: docs/decisions/3822-pocket-ring-scope.md.\n\nFixes #3822\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
